The WildBuzzard Gecko integration is an independent implementation of the
BrowserOS browser-tool contract for Mozilla Gecko.

Principal upstream references:
- packages/browseros-agent/packages/browser-core/src/core/snapshot/
- packages/browseros-agent/packages/browser-mcp/src/tools/
- packages/browseros-agent/crates/browseros-core/src/
- packages/browseros-agent/crates/browseros-mcp/src/

This directory also adapts architecture, lifecycle behavior, and Firefox
protocol integration from Mozilla Firefox DevTools MCP:
https://github.com/mozilla/firefox-devtools-mcp
Upstream revision: 0d7d20017b433cff13d52f8fd57106d9d59087bb
Upstream version: 0.9.15

Firefox DevTools MCP is available under either the MIT License or the Apache
License 2.0. WildBuzzard elects the MIT License for adapted portions. Its
copyright notice and MIT terms are reproduced in MOZILLA-MCP-LICENSE.

Mozilla's public tool names are not exposed as a second model-facing API.
Their Firefox transport, console, network, debugging, download, screenshot,
input, and lifecycle behavior is adapted behind the BrowserOS-compatible
WildBuzzard tool contract.
